PyTorch 2.11-----------------------------

Description
-----------
The module provides a development environment for Artificial
Intelligence(AI)/Machine Learning(ML)/Big Data(BD) on top of Python 3.

Module contents
---------------
Several popular libraries are included in this environment, such as:
    bokeh, matplotlib, mkl, numba, numpy, pandas, pillow, scikit-learn, theano,
pytorch.

To check the full list of available packages in this environment, first
activate it and then run the command
    conda list

* cuda-toolkit 12.6.3
* gpustat 1.1.1
* keras 3.14.0
* matplotlib 3.10.9
* numba 0.65.1
* numpy 2.4.3
* pandas 3.0.2
* pillow 12.1.1
* scikit-image 0.26.0
* scikit-learn 1.8.0
* scipy 1.17.1
* tensorboard 2.20.0
* torch 2.11.0+cu126
* torch-cluster 1.6.3+pt211cu126
* torch-geometric 2.7.0
* torch-scatter 2.1.2+pt211cu126
* torch-sparse 0.6.18+pt211cu126
* torchaudio 2.11.0+cu126
* torchmetrics 1.0.3
* torchvision 0.26.0+cu126
* tqdm 4.66.5
* transformers 5.7.0
* uv 0.11.9

To customize this environment, create an empty venv in a writable directory:
    cd $LOCAL
    # This is using a central Python 3.13 version, feel free to customize as
needed
    uv venv --python /opt/packages/uv/python/cpython-3.13.7-linux-x86_64-gnu

Then activate it, and install the module packages from the original central
environment:
    source .venv/bin/activate
    cp /opt/packages/AI/pytorch_26.05-py3/{pyproject.toml,uv.lock} .
    uv sync --cache-dir $LOCAL/uv_cache --frozen

Finally, proceed with your customization.
    uv pip install PACKAGE # This environment is based on UV.
https://docs.astral.sh/uv/

Module Activation
-------------------
The following commands have been executed for activating the module:
    # source $ENV/bin/activate
    # (/opt/packages/AI/pytorch_26.05-py3) USERNAME@BRIDGES-2:~ $ # << Your
prompt should have changed to something similar.

For deactivating this module, run either of the following commands:
    deactivate
    # or
    module unload AI/pytorch_26.05-py3
